{"text": "Lakeside Women's Health Associates, S.C.\n1500 Sheridan Road, Suite 310 · Wilmette, Illinois 60091 · Tel 847-555-0105 · Fax 847-555-0106\nOctober 21, 2026\nNaveen Chaudhry, MD, MS\nNorthshore University Cancer Genetics Program\nVIA FAX: (847) 555-0199\nRE: GOLDFARB-STEIN, Rivka · DOB 05/28/1987 · our MRN LW-204471\nInsurance: Prairie State Blue Shield PPO, member ID XPS884471205, group 0077418\nDear Dr. Chaudhry:\nI am referring Ms. Goldfarb-Stein, a 39-year-old G2P2 woman, for genetic counseling and management recommendations following a positive result on a multigene panel that I ordered on September 29, 2026.\nResult\nThe laboratory (CLIA-certified; accession no. GX-26-0447182) reported a pathogenic variant in BRCA1, c.68_69delAG, heterozygous. No other reportable variants were identified in the remaining 46 genes. A copy of the report is enclosed.\nFamily history\nMs. Goldfarb-Stein is of Ashkenazi Jewish ancestry on both sides. Her mother, Esther Goldfarb, died of ovarian cancer at age 52. Her sister, Shira, was diagnosed with triple-negative breast cancer at 36 and is in treatment at your institution; I understand she has not had germline testing. A maternal aunt had breast cancer in her sixties. Her father is alive and well at 71. She has two daughters, ages 4 and 7.\nPersonal history\nMenarche at 12; two term deliveries; currently 14 weeks pregnant with an unplanned third pregnancy, which she has not yet disclosed to her employer. No prior breast biopsies. Clinical breast exam on 10/14/2026 was normal. Baseline CA-125 was not drawn because of the pregnancy. She takes levothyroxine 75 mcg daily for Hashimoto's thyroiditis and a prenatal vitamin. She reports significant anxiety since receiving the result and has started seeing a therapist.\nQuestions for you\nTiming of breast MRI surveillance during and after pregnancy, per NCCN.\nCounseling about risk-reducing salpingo-oophorectomy after childbearing.\nCascade testing for her sister, her father and, eventually, her daughters.\nHer concerns about insurance. I explained GINA in general terms; she is worried about life insurance, which GINA does not cover, and asked that the result not be released to anyone, including her husband's employer plan, without her written consent under HIPAA.\nPlease use ICD-10 Z80.41 and the test result for authorization. Rivka prefers to be reached on her personal mobile, 224.555.0167, or at rivka.gs@mailhaven.example, not at work. She observes the Sabbath and cannot take appointments on Friday afternoons or Saturdays.\nMy nurse, Helen Abiodun, RN, can send records: habiodun@lakesidewomens.example, direct line 847-555-0105, extension 4.\nThank you for seeing her.\nSincerely,\nKatarzyna Wiśniewska-Hall, MD, FACOG\nNPI 1447188203 · Illinois license 036.144718\ncc: patient portal", "kind": "Word document", "detail": "415 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Naveen Chaudhry", "Rivka Goldfarb-Stein", "Esther Goldfarb", "Shira", "Katarzyna Wiśniewska-Hall", "Helen Abiodun"], "companies": ["Lakeside Women's Health Associates", "Northshore University Cancer Genetics Program", "Prairie State Blue Shield", "mailhaven.example", "insurance"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Lakeside Women's Health Associates, S.C.", "Wilmette", "Illinois"], "health": ["Hashimoto's thyroiditis", "levothyroxine", "prenatal vitamin", "anxiety", "therapist"], "sensitive": ["Ashkenazi Jewish ancestry", "Ovarian cancer", "Triple-negative breast cancer", "germline testing", "unplanned third pregnancy", "insurance"], "names": ["Naveen", "Rivka", "Esther", "Shira", "Katarzyna", "Helen"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 1, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.5999999940395355, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "crede